# Extra excludes for the EAS build archive (uploaded from the repo root on
# every `eas build`). NOTE: when this file exists, EAS ignores .gitignore
# entirely — so the .gitignore patterns are re-stated first.
#
# Why: EAS honors only a root ignore file, not nested ones (web/.gitignore,
# native/.gitignore), so local build artifacts (web/.next, native/android
# Gradle output) were bloating the upload from ~160 MB of sources to 4+ GB.
# Do NOT add native/google-services.json here — the build needs it, and it
# only uploads because nested .gitignores are skipped.

# --- from root .gitignore ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vercel
node_modules
yarn-error.log
dev
firebase-debug.log
dev-mantic-markets-firebase-adminsdk*.json
mantic-markets-firebase-adminsdk*.json
.env
.env.local

# --- from native/.gitignore: Apple key material + build artifacts ---
# EAS honors only THIS file once it exists, so nested .gitignores never apply and
# these have to be re-stated or they ride along in the upload. iOS builds use
# REMOTE credentials ("ios": {} in eas.json), so Apple key material is never a
# build input and is always safe to drop.
#
# NOT excluded on purpose: credentials.json / *.jks / *.keystore. Android sets
# credentialsSource: "local" on every profile, so those ARE build inputs — adding
# them here would break Android signing. Keep them out of the repo instead.
#
# Also not excluded: native/google-services.json — the build needs it.
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
native/ios/Manifold/GoogleService-Info.plist

# --- build outputs & caches the EAS worker never needs ---
.git/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
native/android/app/build/
native/android/app/.cxx/
native/android/build/
native/android/.gradle/
native/.expo/
native/screenshots/
mani/
